course: dictionary
lesson: 14006
title: Words that give out light
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture for your eyes, and luminous is one of them. It means giving out light, or glowing. «The fish swam through the dark sea, its luminous body glowing blue.» The fish makes its own light, so you can see it in the dark.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Dark, glowing and blue all point to light. Then try the swap test: put your meaning in place of the hard word. «The fish swam through the dark sea, its glowing body glowing blue» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Luminous can also mean very bright and shining, as in «luminous eyes». In informal writing it can describe very bright neon colours, such as a luminous green jacket. The meaning changes a little, but the idea of bright light stays the same.
fact: «Luminous» means giving out light, or glowing.
fact: Luminous objects make their own light, like the Sun, stars, fire and torches.
fact: Non-luminous objects, like the Moon and mirrors, only reflect light.
fact: Luminous vests are bright safety clothing that help drivers see you.
fact: In informal speech, «luminous» can describe very bright neon colours.
exercise: «The deep-sea fish had a luminous glow.» What does luminous mean here? | Very cold to touch | Heavy and slow | *Giving out light, so it glows | Covered in dark mud
exercise: Why do road workers wear luminous vests at night? | *So drivers can see them clearly | To look like the Sun | To keep warm | To hide in the dark
exercise: Which of these is luminous? | The Moon, which only reflects light | A mirror on the wall | A wooden table | *A burning candle
test: «Her luminous eyes shone in the torchlight.» What does luminous suggest about her eyes? | *Bright and shining | Blue, like the sea | Hidden under a hat | Closed and tired
test: Ella says luminous means heavy. Is she right? | Yes, heavy things are always luminous | Only in winter | *No, it means giving out light or glowing | Only in the sea
exam: Which sentence uses luminous correctly? | Her shoes were luminous because they were heavy | The rock was luminous, so it was made of lead | *The stars were luminous in the night sky | The mirror was luminous when the lamp was off
